endobj
119 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 68 0 R
/T (VI. Deadlock as a controlled variation of the same strategy)
/E (VI. Deadlock as a controlled variation of the same strategy)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 68 0 R
/T (Deadlock also supports this argument, even though it is not using a fully public Early Access model. Valve has presented the game as still being in early development, with temporary art and experimental gameplay, while access remains limited. Even so, the logic is similar. Deadlock is a competitive, system-dependent game, so real players are needed to reveal issues with mechanics, tactics, onboarding, and balance before full release.)
/E (Deadlock also supports this argument, even though it is not using a fully public Early Access model. Valve has presented the game as still being in early development, with temporary art and experimental gameplay, while access remains limited. Even so, the logic is similar. Deadlock is a competitive, system-dependent game, so real players are needed to reveal issues with mechanics, tactics, onboarding, and balance before full release.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
