>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (Concord and Highguard can be used as warning cases, although they should not be treated as direct proof that the lack of Early Access alone causes failure. Instead, they suggest that live service and retention sensitive games face significant risk when public iteration is too short, too closed, or treated mainly as marketing.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (A brief beta can help with server testing and awareness, but it is not the same as sustained community led development. For games that depend on long term engagement, public iteration needs to be meaningful enough to expose deeper design problems before launch.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
