133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (Early Access has become an important strategic development model because it helps studios test real player behavior, refine complex systems, and build communities before full release. It is especially useful for games that are balance heavy, economy heavy, or retention sensitive.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (Grinding Gear Games clearly follows this trend. With Path of Exile 2, the studio uses Early Access not simply as promotion, but as a core part of development. This fits the company well because its games depend on deep iteration, long term engagement, and constant system refinement.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (Overall, the rise of Early Access reflects a wider shift in the game industry. Many modern games are no longer finished in isolation and then delivered to players. Instead, they are shaped through an ongoing dialogue between developers and communities.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
